 "notes": "Lower boundary of the combined beam-dump excluded region (union of E137, E141, CHARM and nuCal recasts; dominated by the paper's own E137 recast) in the g_agamma vs m_a plane, figure 2 (left, g_agammaZ=0 scenario). Curve obtained from the e-print ancillary files anc/E137exclusion.dat, E141exclusion.dat, CHARMexclusion.dat, nuCalexclusion.dat, which tabulate log10(prediction/limit) on a grid of log10(m_a/GeV) vs log10(g_agamma/GeV^-1); the boundary is the interpolated zero crossing at the lowest excluded coupling for each mass. Paper convention L = -(g_agamma/4) a F Fdual matches the canonical one. Beam dump bounds are at 95% CL per section 3. The excluded region is a closed blob: its upper edge rises from ~3e-7 GeV^-1 at m~0.5 GeV to above 0.1 GeV^-1 for m<6 MeV (region above the reported curve up to the upper edge is excluded). Belle II curves in the paper are projections and were not used. The paper also derives updated LEP/BaBar/Upsilon/Z-decay and SN1987A bounds; the beam-dump recast is reported as the headline laboratory limit. No DM density assumption (accelerator limit).",
